WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Lend a government 1,000 pounds
by buying one of its bonds.

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.490
It pays you a fixed 50 pounds every year,

3
00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:10.620
then repays the 1,000 at maturity.

4
00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:12.950
You could leave your
money in cash instead,

5
00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:15.630
but cash earns little or nothing.

6
00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:19.260
Yet bond owners sometimes
sell for less than they paid.

7
00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:24.050
In 2022, the Bank of England even
stepped in to buy long-dated government

8
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:27.420
bonds. So why would anyone
sell a safe government

9
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.970
bond for less than they paid for it?

10
00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.050
In this mission, you'll meet savers,

11
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:36.170
borrowers, shares and bonds,
and see how they connect.

12
00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:38.350
Then you'll use a graph lab to test what

13
00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:40.240
moves a bond's price.

14
00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.890
Your mission: find out what
sets the price of a bond.
